        "biography": "",
        "appearance": "",
        "notes": "<h5>Opportunities and Complications</h5><p><strong>Opportunity.</strong> An enemy can spend <span class=\"cosmere-icon opportunity-color\">O</span> to prevent the outlaw boss from using their Rile ’Em Up action and Don’t Disappoint Me reaction until the end of the outlaw boss’s next turn.</p><p><strong>Complication.</strong> The GM can spend <span class=\"cosmere-icon complication-color\">C</span> from an enemy’s test to have the outlaw boss use their Get ’Em, Boys! action as <span class=\"cosmere-icon\">r</span>.</p><h5>Tactics</h5><p>An <strong>outlaw boss</strong> coordinates their subordinate outlaws with their Get ’Em, Boys! action. Outlaw bosses with low regard for their minions aren’t afraid to fire into a busy melee with Reckless Menace. Later in a combat, outlaw bosses use their Rile ’Em Up action to help allied outlaws recover enough focus to graze or to use their Roughhousing action.</p>",
        "role": "boss"
    },
